From 73d2b16b87e077a889f546e0c80a9d40a796c3be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:16:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): cameras by libcamera id, IR/colour/both modes,
 every camera's faces, test scan

For laptops whose IR and colour cameras sit behind one CSI-2 receiver
(Snapdragon X: they share all their /dev/video nodes) face login can
now be set up in the app alone:

- Cameras: the camera pickers list libcamera's cameras by id
  (biopass-helper list-cameras; IR = monochrome sensor), then video
  devices that belong to none of them. A mode sets `camera`,
  `anti_spoofing.ir_camera` and `ir_recognition`: ir (the IR camera
  recognises; AI anti-spoofing off, its models are trained on colour
  pictures), rgb (colour recognises, IR presence check), both (each
  recognises against its own faces). Choosing one writes a minimum face
  size of 0.2 and a threshold of 0.6 where the settings have none or a
  looser one. The settings page edits these fields and never writes
  camera profiles any more; profiles of an earlier save are read as
  the camera settings and replaced on save. The minimum face size has
  a slider, the threshold a hint.
- Faces: each camera keeps its own (faces/ the main camera's, faces-ir/
  the IR camera's while the colour camera is the main one, faces-rgb/
  the colour camera's while the IR camera is). Saving a change between
  the IR and the colour camera as the main camera moves them
  (face::move_faces_for_main_camera) and says so. The page lists every
  directory, labelled by camera and whether this mode uses it, with
  delete and delete all (re-enrolling). Enrolment uses the saved
  settings' cameras: in both mode each picture is a pair, the colour
  camera's into faces/ and the IR camera's into faces-ir/ (the preview
  switches cameras: they stream one at a time); "Add 5" takes five,
  two seconds apart. The preview restarts on another camera.
- Test: one `biopass-helper auth --verbose --keep-looking 6000` with the
  saved settings shows the outcome (match, no match, no face, not
  tried), the steps (face size against the minimum, scores) and each
  compared face's best score on its picture, red when not above the
  threshold: faces that do not score well against the user are easy to
  find and replace. The asset scope adds faces-ir/ and faces-rgb/.
Tests: cameras, face (sets, moves, deletes), scan (steps, scores),
config, webview_security, faceMode.test.ts, selectValue.test.ts.
